<h2 class="wp-block-heading">In the Community</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><a href="https://macsparky.circle.so/c/labs-discussion-board/beta-ios-27-or-not">Beta iOS 27 or not</a></strong> (Labs Discussion Board)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A member heading out on holiday asked whether putting the iOS 27 public beta on an iPhone 15 Pro Max was going to be a regret. Mostly he wanted to try the new Siri. The replies were encouraging. People running it since beta 2 called it one of Apple&#8217;s steadier betas, with the rough spots showing up as widgets going dark, shortcut automations that need rebuilding, and the occasional freeze a restart clears. The one real caution was about the Mac, where Golden Gate has been rougher than iOS has been on the phone.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><a href="https://macsparky.circle.so/c/labs-discussion-board/plaud-users-new-mcp-and-cli-functionality">Plaud users &#8211; new MCP and CLI functionality</a></strong> (Labs Discussion Board)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A member passed along word that the company behind the Plaud audio recorder has shipped both an MCP server and a command line tool. That is the interesting part. Getting recordings and transcripts out of Plaud&#8217;s own app and into wherever you actually keep your notes, Obsidian or NotePlan included, stops being a manual chore.</p>



